## Pipeline:

IF: 
- Make the memory request for the instruction
- Determine the next PC

ID:
- Decode instruction and set all control signals
- Read from the register file

EX1:
- the alu computes in this cycle
- this means: adresses are generated, branches are resolved, and alu ops are computed

EX2 (mem reads):
- mem reads and writes

RET:
- currently everything is in-order, so only write-back to the register file
- later: retire in-order

## Branch predictor
Start with the most simple:
1. BTB  (PC -> target)
    - 256 entries
    - uses 8 LSB of PC as index, no tag, but a valid bit
    - each entry is updated with a new target every time a branch/jump is taken
2. Saturating 2-bit counters
    - 128 entries
    - uses 7 LSB of PC as index, no tag
    - each entry is updated when a branch is resolved

